 "note": [
  "Thomas weaves Scripture into his sentences, usually from the Latin Vulgate and rarely with a reference. Where he quotes a verse and Kulish (1905, ebible ukr_pan via the GitHub mirror) says the same, Kulish is pasted verbatim in its own orthography; where his wording follows the Vulgate or re-persons the verse, it is rendered from the English and marked self_rendered. Mined rows were machine-checked as verbatim substrings of the Kulish text.",
  "AI-translated (job #7624) in eleven parallel chapter ranges against one shared term table, then reconciled. Divine pronouns are capitalized (Ти/Твій; Christ’s own Я/Мій in Books III–IV), as in confessions.uk. Three quotations with no single identifiable source verse (ch. 61 the command to the north wind, ch. 90 “I have sinned, O Lord…”, ch. 95 “I yet live, says the Lord…”) carry no row. Awaiting native review."
